# Agent settings that every push applies to /etc/prohori.env (infra/push.sh) and that bootstrap.sh / bootstrap_cool.sh start with,
# so a rebuilt box and a pushed box agree.  Decision and evidence: research/AGENT_PREREG.md Addendum B, eval/results/agent_ablation.md.
# Default policy is the LLM agent behind the deterministic guardrail (agent.py).  Rules take over when the daily cap is used up,
# when no Bedrock model answers, or when the model's chosen action breaks a hard rule twice.
# Primary model: Nova Lite.  Claude Haiku 4.5 (us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0) was the pre-registered challenger (P3) but this AWS
# account has not submitted Anthropic's model use case form, so Bedrock answers ResourceNotFoundException; P3 was not evaluated and the
# pre-registered rule keeps Nova Lite primary.  To switch after the form is approved: set Haiku as AGENT_BEDROCK_MODEL, Nova Lite as fallback.
AGENT_POLICY=llm
AGENT_BEDROCK_MODEL=us.amazon.nova-lite-v1:0
AGENT_BEDROCK_FALLBACK_MODELS=us.amazon.nova-micro-v1:0
AGENT_LLM_DAILY_CAP=200
